From ae9d0a3b21d2f85f6f73e00bfb0e8ef29725ac6d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 03:57:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] PETSc: Krylov solver and preconditioner in the factories

PETScLinearSolver (KSP) and PETScPreconditioner (PC) are configured by
the options of PETSc given by their Options parameter, written in the
options database with a prefix unique to each solver and removed when
the solver is destroyed; the options never read by PETSc are reported.
The tolerances of mfem-mgis are overridden by the options of PETSc. A
preconditioner of another library is a shell preconditioner of PETSc,
which receives the operators; PETScPreconditioner becomes the
preconditioner of the Krylov solver, and may be used by the Krylov
solvers of MFEM. The options of the preconditioner of PETSc are refused
in the options of a solver given a preconditioner.

PETSc is initialized when the first solver of PETSc is built, and
finalized by finalize, unless the program initialized it.
